rua-tool — notes for the Debian/Kali packager
==============================================

Go version
----------
The upstream go.mod declares `go 1.26.0`. That floor comes *only* from the
pinned standalone dependency `golang.org/x/net v0.63.0` (the latest, CVE-free
release), not from this tool's own code.

rua-tool's own source uses no Go 1.23+ language features and only long-stable
`x/net` APIs:
  * golang.org/x/net/publicsuffix  — EffectiveTLDPlusOne
  * golang.org/x/net/html          — NewTokenizer / Token / token kinds
  * golang.org/x/net/idna          — Lookup.ToASCII

It has been verified to compile with **Go 1.22** against **x/net as old as
v0.25.0**. So when built the Debian way — in GOPATH mode against the packaged
`golang-golang-x-net-dev` rather than the network-pinned module — the Go 1.26
toolchain is not required; the distro's Go (>= 1.22) and its `x/net` suffice.
This is why debian/control uses an unversioned `golang-any` build-dependency.

If a module-mode build insists on the go.mod directive, either build in GOPATH
mode or lower the directive for the package build; no source changes are needed.

x/net version
-------------
The code does not depend on any `x/net` API newer than v0.25.0, so whatever
version `golang-golang-x-net-dev` provides in the target suite will work.

Validation status
-----------------
Built locally with `dpkg-buildpackage -b` using Debian's golang-go (1.22) in
GOPATH mode against golang-golang-x-net-dev 1:0.21.0 (so neither Go 1.26 nor the
pinned x/net was needed). lintian reports only `initial-upload-closes-no-bugs`
(expected for a first package, ignorable for a non-Debian target); the binary is
built with -buildmode=pie. Please still run a final sbuild + lintian on a Kali
builder with the kali vendor profile; see docs/kali-submission.md.
